{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>\"And I will hear, for I am gracious\"</b> — He is gracious (חַנּוּן) and accepts the plea of every person, even one who is not deserving, from the root חִנָּם (gratuitous favor). The meaning is: do not think, \"I will not seize the garment of the righteous, but the garment of a person who is not righteous I will take and not return, for his cry will not be heard by El.\" Therefore He said, <b>\"for I am gracious\"</b>, and I hear the cry of everyone who pleads to Me:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:14:19.076992251Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}